From: Grizbeard <justin.morken@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:45:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] Draw bars on the beat grid, numbered, and let the
 downbeat move

[AI-generated text: this description was written autonomously by an AI
agent (Claude). Review it before relying on it or submitting it.]

A skin that sets DownbeatColor gets every fourth beat, counted from the
beat grid's first marker, drawn 2 px wide in that colour, and bar numbers
along the top of the waveform (BarNumberColor, BarNumberFont,
BarNumberSize). Numbers that would collide are thinned to every 2nd, 4th,
... bar. Skins without DownbeatColor look as before. Only the allshader
waveforms draw bars.

Mixxx detects no downbeats, so bar 1 is wherever the grid starts: the
first beat the analyser found, or the first marker of an imported Serato
grid. [ChannelN],beats_downbeat_earlier/_later move it by one beat with
Beats::tryMoveFirstMarker(), which moves no beat, so it is saved with the
grid and allowed on BPM-locked tracks too.

DigitsRenderNode gains a colour, a font and any number of labels for this.

Tested on Windows: the beat unit tests, new ones included, pass, and
Terminal-wide shows numbered bars on a 120 BPM test track.

[End of AI-generated text.]

